# Exposure and source coverage

This is a source-exposed comparison of the new root local-bias proof with an earlier frozen derivation by the same worker/model family. It is not an audit and does not supply a second independent research lineage for already shared circuit, Gibbs-interface or quantum-comparison machinery.

The independent packet's exact seal is `d5863f3f2955e8c840567c37275bd6955d6a8661ad29795149985af8a8ddad27`, with recorded sealing time 2026-10-15T16:57:05.319798+00:00. The actual tool clock immediately before first reading the root proof and mandatory qualification was 2026-10-15 16:58:59 UTC. This timing statement reports that observed tool result; it is not a newly invented pre-reading launch receipt. The two sources were read completely, without truncated coverage, and their exact bytes are copied once in `source/`.

The root proof `637ccbabb9d275bffd3bc53c857d873ecc9ab3e7fd492600ef7d819b598c9b95` has 103 lines. Complete coverage includes all five sections and all equations (1)–(9). The 1,801-byte later qualification `c5cc61346fe3d44bf3ec25142f9c98e480cec8678b6ca70b53f4760dbe7f153e` was also read completely. Subsequent targeted rereading covered the entire short root proof and the independent source's necessity/counterexamples, endpoint construction, full marginal comparison, quench/composition, counts, precision, moments and work. No root-source statement was accepted simply from its author's status or later commentary.

The independent 38,107-byte derivation was authored and read in full before its freeze. Its existing complete accepted-source coverage remains valid at unchanged identities. Current metadata checks refresh all seven prior source/recovery pairs and the three instruction identities. They verify all 31 independent freeze members unchanged, but do not relabel those hash checks as new scientific reviews.

Prior exposure to the earlier composition source `6296fd36b048b030a07f87be41838ce1f03c1f523442b63484b239f5173f2c3f` during the PR9608 scope task is retained. That source was not reopened or used as an accepted proof dependency here. The new local-bias root candidate had not been read, inventoried, hashed or searched before the independent freeze. Neither optional noncommuting-boundary source nor any rotated-Gibbs or later composition candidate was opened during this comparison.

The shared prior sources cover the original fixed geometry and isolation inventory, returned dirty routing and gate phases, majority tree, full unconditioned-marginal lemma, compensated readiness, actual-time target, moment/work accounts and Gibbs switch. Their reuse is stated explicitly; only the new local conditional-bias argument and its compatibility are compared here. The exact frozen predecessor root decision is metadata provenance, not mathematical evidence by itself. Its separate `VERIFICATION.json` was not newly inspected.

No new external scientific source was opened for this comparison. The independent packet's limited stochastic-domination reference reading remains separately recorded there. The root qualification's Holley reference is reported with its original reading limitation; it was not independently checked here or substituted for the elementary finite coupling proof.

No scientific program, numerical diagnostic, sweep, formal checker or previous science replay was run. Source capture and metadata verification record their actual child-process launches, script hashes, output hashes, exit statuses and timestamps under `metadata_runs/`. No failures occurred in those captured executions. The sealer's source and actual tool completion are separate from the two child-process receipts; it does not invent an execution receipt for itself.

The independent packet, root sources, science checkout, Git/PR state, audit state, checkpoints, locks, axioms and editable prompts are unchanged. All new files are below this comparison directory. No additional agent was spawned and no model or reasoning-effort override was selected. Communication was limited to the parent task.
